      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T18:54:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So, the question that I have is why this optimization is not working for your android builds?\n\nclang-r530567 is a new clang build that hasn\u0027t been released. It enables frame pointer by default for x86_64 android build (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/97614). That makes do_full_int80() sets up frame pointer even when optimized with -O2. You can try it in https://android.googlesource.com/platform/prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/+/refs/heads/main/clang-r530567/.",
      "parentUuid": "61a1ec1a_ab895ea7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1960,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1960,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "079ccd46c7db755ebb2399eddca864c43f535066",
